.TH SET_TID_ADDRESS 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
set_tid_address \- sets the calling thread clear-child-tid address and returns its thread id
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_extra.h>
.B pid_t set_tid_address(int* address);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets the calling thread clear-child-TID address and returns its thread ID. The kernel writes zero and performs a futex wake at thread exit, so the address must remain writable until then. This changes thread runtime state.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR set_tid_address (2)
